  "subtitle": "Golden egg-soaked bread",
  "excerpt": "French toast is made by soaking thick slices of bread in a spiced egg and cream mixture, then frying in butter until golden. Stale bread works best because it soaks up the custard without falling apart. Serve with honey and a dusting of icing sugar.",
